course: dictionary
lesson: 8922
title: Sienna: a colour and a name
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Sienna is a word with two jobs. Most of the time it is a colour, a brownish-yellow or reddish-brown like earth, tree trunks and autumn leaves. Artists use it in paints and crayons.
explain: Sienna can also be a girl's first name. How do you tell which one it is? Look for clues. In «Sienna's huge house», the capital S and the 's show that Sienna owns the house, so Sienna is a name.
explain: Look at the words around it. «Burnt sienna» and «raw sienna» are colours, so when sienna comes after burnt or raw, it is the colour. Always ask: does the sentence still make sense if I swap in a colour, or if I put in a person's name?
fact: Sienna is a colour: raw sienna is brownish-yellow and burnt sienna is reddish-brown.
fact: Sienna is also a clay pigment, the stuff that makes the colour. It was first dug near Siena in Italy.
fact: Sienna is also a girl's first name, as in «Sienna in Melbourne won her race».
fact: A capital letter in the middle of a sentence is a clue that a word is a name.
fact: Art lessons use «burnt sienna» and «raw sienna» for tree trunks, skin tones, earth and autumn leaves.
exercise: «Burnt sienna» is a paint colour. What kind of colour is it? | A bright blue like the sea | A soft, pale pink | A shiny silver metal | *A reddish-brown earth colour
exercise: In «Sienna's huge house», is Sienna a colour or a name? | A colour | *A name | A kind of paint | A type of clay
exercise: «Sienna in Melbourne won her race and swam over to the last girl.» What is Sienna here? | A colour of paint | *A girl's name | A town in Australia | A kind of tree
test: What does the capital S in the middle of a sentence tell you? | The sentence is a question | *A person's name is coming | It is the start of a new paragraph | A new colour has started
test: What is the clay pigment that gives sienna its colour? | Chalk dust from a school board | Sand from a beach | Limestone from a quarry in Scotland | *Clay first dug near Siena in Italy
exam: Maya reads «The walls of the café were painted burnt sienna.» What does burnt sienna describe? | A girl who lives in Italy | *A reddish-brown colour | A type of cake sold at the café | A loud noise from the kitchen
